  "purpose": "declared directional traverse of the wall corridor, the one measurement the balanced probe cannot take. In the wall corridor south is responsive while north is not (the analysed grid reads 0.1527 against 0.0000 at 16:13), so a balanced eight-direction schedule cancels less well in one axis and its own pulses walk the hero away from the wall: the v14 run covered 16:12 through 23:12, south of the stall, and 15:13 still held a single sample. This contract therefore declares the subset it presses - north, north_east and north_west - and gives up cancellation on purpose, so the pulses spend the wall slide on the corridor under test. pulses_per_direction is six and control_windows six so the footprint stays a short line west along the wall rather than spreading over many cells, and maximum_cells_with_bearing_observations is declared at eight for a sweep; the honest check on the result is the per-cell sample counts the grid reports, not that cap. The press subset is a declared choice for this instrument, not a threshold relaxed after a run. This version doubles the pulse count so the same wall slide covers about four cells west instead of two, and declares the concentration cap at ten upfront for the longer sweep; everything else is unchanged.",
  "schedule_seed": 23,
